%% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
%% CAPTION
%%
%% What this shows: the five kinds of evidence this project accepts, and the
%% one path each is allowed to take. Only MASS becomes the number the model
%% learns from. COUNT can become that number ONLY when a real mean nodule mass
%% was recorded with the sample — otherwise it stays a count. COVER is the
%% strict one: a percent-cover reading is never turned into kg per square
%% metre, because doing so would invent a mass nobody measured. GRID surfaces
%% (TS-6, Washburn) are used to CHECK the model, never to train it, which is
%% what keeps the final benchmark comparison honest. GRADE carries the metal
%% chemistry and joins onto a station.
%%
%% Why it matters: these rules are the project's scientific backbone, and they
%% are enforced by code and tests rather than by convention — a COVER row that
%% carried an abundance value would fail validation and stop the build. The
%% screening step flags implausible values but never deletes them: nothing
%% disappears silently, and a flagged row stays in the corpus for audit while
%% being kept out of training.
%%
%% Numbers on this diagram: 36 MASS rows, of which 35 are training-eligible
%% (one box core, SO268/1_12-2, was flagged as a failed recovery). Screening
%% bounds 0-45 kg_m2 come from data/config/normalization.yaml.
